ass=3D"sc-ilnrqe fWuETc"><h2>File descriptions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>train.csv</strong> - the training set</li>
<li><strong>test.csv</strong> - the test set</li>
<li><strong>example-submission.csv</strong> - a sample submission file in t=
he correct format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Data fields</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>RENT_APPROVAL_DATE</strong> - year and month when the rent was =
approved as string, e.g., "2021-01" representing January 2021</li>
<li><strong>TOWN</strong> - the town of the sold HDB flat (e.g., "Bishan", =
"Queenstown", "Clementi")</li>
<li><strong>BLOCK</strong> - block number of the flat (e.g.,  "300", "306A"=
, "254")</li>
<li><strong>STREET</strong> - street name of block containing the flat (e.g=
.,  "ubi avenue 1", "woodlands drive 14")</li>
<li><strong>FLAT_TYPE</strong> - type of flat (e.g.,  "2 room", "3 room", "=
4-room")</li>
<li><strong>FLAT_MODEL</strong> - model of the flat (e.g., "model a", "dbss=
", ''executive")</li>
<li><strong>FLOOR_AREA_SQM</strong> - floor area in square meter (e.g., 104=
.0, 74.0, 136.0)</li>
<li><strong>FURNISHED</strong> - indicator if flat is furnished ("yes" or "=
no")</li>
<li><strong>LEASE_COMMENCE_DATE</strong> - year the lease for flat commence=
d (e.g., 1984, 1985, 1986)</li>
<li><strong>FEE</strong> - additional upfront fee of rental agreement (e.g.=
, 200, 300, 400)</li>
<li><strong>MONTHLY_RENT</strong> - rental rate SGD (e.g., 2350, 4000, 3200=
)</li>
</ul>
<h2>Auxiliary Data</h2>
<p>The folder auxiliary-data contains additional data files that might help=
 to improve the predictions. Most files contain the location of places of i=
nterest incl. MRT stations (open and planned), shopping malls, and schools.=
 The intuition this that the prices of a resale flat might (strongly) depen=
d, for example, on the distance to the nearest MRT station. Other data incl=
ude the about <a href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Certificate_of_Entit=
lement" rel=3D"noreferrer nofollow">Certificate of Entitlement (COE)</a> pr=
ices, as well as the stock prices for the <a href=3D"https://companiesmarke=
tcap.com/sgd/singapore/largest-companies-in-singapore-by-market-cap/" rel=
=3D"noreferrer nofollow">largest companies in Singepore by market cap</a>. =
Both COE and stock prices cover the same date range as the one from the mai=
n rental dataset</p>
<p>There are many ways to use these information to derive new features for =
the training process. It is up to you to decide how which information to us=
e in what way. You can also decide not use certain information, or some par=
ts of it (e.g., considering only the 50 most popular malls instead of all).=
 The important part is to argue and justify your decisions.</p>
<h2>Additional Data Collection</h2>
<p>You are more then welcome to collect your own data to potentially genera=
te more useful data. Maybe the traffic and travel times are an deciding fac=
tor; LTA provide an API to collect these information in real-time. Please b=
e aware, however, that data collection has it's challenges, particularly if=
 the data cannot be simply downloaded (one-time download of historical data=
 vs. collecting real-time data over several days or weeks).</p></div></div>=
